## Portfolio overview

| Priority | Research idea | Primary mechanism | Bedside nurse workload |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Automated transition-friction detection | Finds unresolved barriers before discharge | Neutral or reduced |
| 2 | Actionability-based readmission targeting | Sends patients to the right intervention | Reduced unnecessary referrals |
| 3 | Community pharmacy medication rescue | Moves reconciliation after discharge to pharmacists | Reduced |
| 4 | Exception-only virtual ward | Automates routine monitoring and escalates only deterioration | Neutral |
| 5 | CHW “last-mile” support | Addresses transportation, food, housing, and appointment barriers | Reduced |
| 6 | Discharge instruction co-pilot | Improves comprehension without extra teaching time | Neutral |
| 7 | ED-to-home rescue pathway | Prevents avoidable admission after post-discharge ED use | Neutral |
| 8 | Caregiver capacity matching | Matches support intensity to actual caregiving ability | Reduced |
| 9 | Post-acute handoff reliability system | Ensures SNF/home-health receipt and action | Neutral |
| 10 | Readmission learning loop | Converts readmission causes into targeted system fixes | Minimal |

